@host = http://localhost:5092
@id = 01a0481c-b0cf-7877-9537-354ad5a67244

### 0. Upload a file first (paste the returned id into @id above)
POST {{host}}/api/file
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----Boundary

------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./../uploads/2026/08/25/01a039cd4c207291af6be0f9ce5e324c.png
------Boundary--

### 1. Download — no resolution param (defaults to null)
GET {{host}}/api/file/{{id}}

### 2. Download — resolution=original (case-insensitive enum name)
GET {{host}}/api/file/{{id}}?resolution=original

### 3. Download — resolution=thumbnail
GET {{host}}/api/file/{{id}}?resolution=thumbnail

### 4. Download — resolution=small
GET {{host}}/api/file/{{id}}?resolution=small

### 5. Download — resolution=medium
GET {{host}}/api/file/{{id}}?resolution=medium

### 6. Download — resolution=large
GET {{host}}/api/file/{{id}}?resolution=large

### 7. Download — resolution=extraLarge
GET {{host}}/api/file/{{id}}?resolution=extraLarge

### 8. Download — resolution by numeric value (2 = Small)
GET {{host}}/api/file/{{id}}?resolution=2

### 9. Download — invalid resolution string (should 400)
GET {{host}}/api/file/{{id}}?resolution=huge

### 10. Download — non-guid id (should 400 from route constraint)
GET {{host}}/api/file/not-a-guid

### 11. Download — well-formed guid that doesn't exist (should 404)
GET {{host}}/api/file/99999999-9999-9999-9999-999999999999

### 12. Exists check — HEAD (200 or 404, no body)
HEAD {{host}}/api/file/{{id}}
